error BYN2201: a `string` cannot be indexed

  2 │ let first = name[0];
    │                 ^^^ strings have no indexer
    │
  help: `string` is UTF-8, so position 0 is not a character. Choose what you mean:
          `name.bytes[0]`   the byte at offset 0 (applied below)
          `name.runeAt(0)`  the character starting at byte offset 0
          `for (let c in name)`   each character in turn
          `name.graphemes`        user-perceived characters
    │ 2 │ let first = name.bytes[0];
